From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 01:31:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/25] Bulk-ingest the Rgveda-Pratishakhya sutra text (all
 1,067 sutras)

With the lead's go-ahead, pulls the full Sanskrit Library LoadText
endpoint (see tools/pratishakhya/SOURCES.md) rather than just the
single inspection fetch from the previous commit, and writes all 18
patalas into rigveda_pratishakhya/data.json following this repo's usual
one-data.json-per-work convention (not the per-patala-file layout
sketched earlier). Patala 10 (Krama) = 22 sutras, patala 11 (Kramahetu)
= 71 -- exactly matching the secondary sources already cross-checked.
258 of 1,067 sutras carry the source's own OCR-uncertainty marker and
are shipped with has_uncertain_reading=true and empty Devanagari/IAST
rather than a guessed reading.

Building the real importer caught a mistake in the architecture doc's
own earlier verified-sample table -- sutra 10.20 had been quoted as
only its second clause, and 10.20/10.22 had their source-marked "[?]"
characters silently guessed as "u" -- both fixed with a correction note
rather than quietly overwritten. Also updates library.json (populated:
true), adds tests/test_rv_pratishakhya_import.py, and marks the
architecture doc's and PENDING.md's blocking prerequisite resolved.

